                     /inference="protein motif:Pfam:IPR003723"
                     /note="CobK/CbiJ; there are 2 pathways for cobalamin
                     (vitamin B12) production, one aerobic (ex. P.
                     denitrificans), the other anaerobic (ex. S. typhimurium);
                     the CobK/CbiJ perform similar reactions in both; the
                     anaerobic pathway includes the use of a chelated cobalt
                     ion in order for ring contraction to occur; CobK thus
                     converts precorrin 6 into dihydro-precorrin 6 while CbiJ
                     converts cobalt-precorrin 6 into cobalt-deihydro-precorrin
                     6"
